Kafka Producer and Consumer Terminal Setup Guide

Prerequisite:
Ensure that ZooKeeper and the Kafka broker are running in the background of your virtual machine.

Step 1: Open the first terminal for the Producer
- Open terminal window number one.
- Run the following command to start the Kafka console producer, pointing it to the local broker and specifying the topic name:
  kafka-console-producer --broker-list localhost:9092 --topic ironhack
- Press Enter to see the `>` prompt waiting for text input.

Step 2: Open the second terminal for the Consumer
- Open a second, separate terminal window.
- Run the following command to start the Kafka console consumer, connecting it to ZooKeeper, targeting the same topic, and using `--from-beginning` to catch all messages:
  kafka-console-consumer --zookeeper localhost:2181 --topic ironhack --from-beginning
- Press Enter.

Step 3: Test the Communication
- Click back into your Producer terminal and type messages (e.g., hello, this is a producer), pressing Enter after each.
- View the Consumer terminal on the right to see the messages appear in real time.
